.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-egress-change-approve - Approve the pending egress change


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container egress-change approve  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Approve the pending egress change

.PP
Continue now: the new nodes start taking traffic, the old ones are drained and removed. \fBid\fR (optional) must match \fBegress_change.id\fR (409 \fBchange_mismatch\fR when a newer change replaced it). 409 \fBno_pending_change\fR / \fBchange_preparing\fR\&. Every change of a dedicated environment's node set (plan change, extra node added or removed) is announced BEFORE the old nodes go: as soon as the new nodes' addresses are known (usually under a minute) the owner is notified (Alerts channels, event \fBegress\fR) and \fBegress_change\fR / \fBpending_egress_ips\fR show them. With the approval step on (\fBPUT /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-approval\fR, 1-72 hours, 24 recommended) the new nodes take no traffic and the old nodes keep serving until \fBPOST /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-change/approve\fR or the deadline (then it continues by itself). A removal only never waits.

.PP
API: POST /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-change/approve (operationId approveContainerEgressChange, scope services_write)


